    resolves through the refresh impl: rotated access/refresh persisted,
    request shape (`grant_type=refresh_token`, refresh_token, client_id).
  - `zen_refresh_invalid_grant_reports_reconnect` — HTTP 400
    `invalid_grant` → "Reconnect OpenCode Console to continue".

## Final report

Landed (auditE-core #1 — the whole provider-login pipeline):
- oc-core `integration` host: registry + credential store + OAuth
  (device + code + PKCE-loopback engines) + command/env sourcing + refresh
  + scrub lifecycle + `integration.updated`; Engine boots it.
- Providers: catalog key/env (azure filter), zen/OpenCode Console device
  + refresh + orgName label, GitHub Copilot device (enterprise form,
  entitlement, key-method removal), xAI device + refresh, DigitalOcean
  implicit (port 1456), Poe code+PKCE.
- oc-server: 11 routes live over the host with v2 error mapping;
  wellknown discovery + kv persistence + boot re-registration.
- CLI: `oc auth login/list/logout` e2e green against a real spawned
  server (zen flow via mock IdP + hidden `server` answer).
- Events: credential.updated/switched published through the shared bus
  (SSE-verified); integration.updated registered + published.

Verification: fmt + clippy (pedantic) clean; nextest 1184→1188/1188
across oc-core + oc-server + oc-cli (0 failures); no oc-tui changes.

Deferred remainder (for successor lanes):
- OAuth flows not ported: chatgpt browser/headless token-sharing,
  azure Entra ID (CLI), gitlab, snowflake external-browser, openai codex
  variants (each needs its own authorize/refresh pair on the same host
  skeleton — providers.rs is the extension point).
- Copilot provider TRANSPORT (token exchange → Copilot API bearer,
  models sync, responses prep) — the audit's separate "no copilot
  binding in facade.rs" row; auth host hands out the credential only.
- Wellknown `config`/`remote_config` resolution into the provider config
  graph (config.ts:292-311) — the config lane's surface.
- Zen remote provider catalog ingestion (console /providers → provider
  overlay), managed policy statements, Console MCP servers — consumer
  side of the console credential.
- v2's runtime `connection.status` reporting by provider plugins
  (needs_auth projection) is plumbed but no reporter is wired yet.
